# Force LF line endings on checkout regardless of platform. Without this,
# Git for Windows' common default (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites every
# tracked text file to CRLF the moment it's checked out -- which then makes
# `git status` see every single file as "modified" from the LF version
# actually committed, even though the user never touched anything. That
# directly broke self-update for a real Windows user: `apply_update`'s
# safety check (only pulls on a clean checkout) refused every single
# attempt with "Local changes exist in the repo checkout," for a week,
# because of line endings alone -- silently blocking them from ever
# receiving a fix again, including this one. Every text file in this repo
# is already stored as LF (verified directly, including install.ps1 and
# doi_host.bat), so this doesn't change anything for existing clones -- it
# only stops a *future* Windows clone from drifting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch line endings, ever.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
